# Write-tier negative: a NON-NFC literal NESTED inside an RDF-1.2 triple-term object. The base
# "cafe" followed by U+0301 (combining acute accent) — authored with an explicit Turtle \uXXXX
# escape so the non-canonical spelling survives editor/VCS normalization — rides in the object
# slot of the nested triple <<( s p o )>>, so the top-level quad object is a triple term, NOT a
# bare literal. gmn1_write must walk INTO the triple term and hard-fail
# (lang:GmnNonCanonicalCodepoint) before any record is built — never letting the nested
# non-canonical spelling reach the content-digest layer.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

gmeow:someAgent gmeow:asserts <<( gmeow:noteX gmeow:statusLabel "cafe\u0301"^^xsd:string )>> .
